WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:05.531
Whatever the browser can draw, the race goes on.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.741
Where neither WebGPU nor WebGL two can draw, the map's panorama takes the world's

00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:18.114
place, and the race still runs.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.312
Switch tabs, and the world stops drawing. The race clock and your power carry on.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.803
Main's loop already stopped, but the scene still drew a frame each time the clock

00:00:35.803 --> 00:00:38.847
ticked. Now a hidden tab draws nothing at all.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:45.383
Come back, and the world draws again, the race twenty seconds further on.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.011
From a phone to a desktop, the panorama fills the screen behind the race.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.813
What the tests prove: a hidden tab draws no frame while the race runs on, and shown

00:01:06.813 --> 00:01:08.052
again, it draws.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
